ed stripped-envelope tail. The Ibc fit at z equals 0.15 reproduces this post-peak decline with chi2 per point 0.41 and places peak about 35 days before now.", "hypothesis": "ibc", "refuted_if": {"band": "ztfr", "day": 3, "direction": "above", "flux": 160, "why": "A 40-day-old stripped-envelope tail must keep fading in r, so a rise back to plateau-peak brightness would need a fresh power source."}, "weakest_point": "The r-band limit at minus 6.6 d to 19.3 mag is about one magnitude fainter than detections bracketing it at minus 11.5 and minus 0.5 d, implying a dip and rebrightening unlike a smooth supernova tail."}], "weights": {"ia": 0.4639, "ibc": 0.0526, "ii": 0.3713, "null": 0.1123}, "wording": {"term": "unlikely", "text": "It is unlikely that this distant flash will look brighter than the specified level in red light 3 days from now.", "words_match": true}}, "prev": "123b3602ba9bcac4efd8fdeeeba369a9d37df021bad13d8d55da9f53d52bbdbe", "seq": 10, "time": "2022-08-14T19:06:23+00:00", "v": 2}
